# python
__pycache__/

# LoRA adapter weights. 120 MB per epoch checkpoint, 626 MB for one five-epoch
# run — git is the wrong home for them and they are reproducible from the
# receipt beside them (seed, data SHA-256, every hyperparameter, package
# versions, GPU). What DOES get committed from a run is run-config.json and the
# prediction JSONLs: kilobytes, and the only part anyone needs to check a claim.
# Publish adapters to a Hugging Face model repo, the way jam-ft-v1 was.
# Any depth under runs/: the second v1 run landed at runs/v20/seed13/epoch3/,
# one level deeper than the first, and the single-star pattern would have let
# 376 MB of adapters into a commit. Checked with git add -n before staging;
# that check is why this line exists.
experiments/**/runs/**/epoch*/
experiments/**/runs/**/hf-out/
